+## Inspect a presentation
+
+Capture a settled production-preview screenshot for every step and review advisory visual diagnostics:
+
+```bash
+npm run inspect -- how-to-make-a-presentation
+npm run inspect -- how-to-make-a-presentation --viewport 390x844 --settle 1600
+```
+
+The helper builds when `dist/` is missing or stale. Use `--no-build` to require an existing current build, `--settle <ms>` to set the wait after each step (default 1200), `--viewport WxH` to choose a browser viewport (default 1440x900), or `--port <port>` to select the preview port. By default, screenshots capture only the configured viewport; pass `--full-page` to capture the whole document. Screenshots are written to `.presentation-inspection/<slug>/step-NN.png`; that directory is ignored by Git. Warnings identify likely overlap, indistinct active navigation, or attribution styling issues and remain advisory. If two elements intentionally overlap, mark their shared subtree with `data-presentation-allow-overlap`; only use the marker when the composition remains readable. Attribution should be styled through `data-presentation-attribution`, with at least an 11px font and 24px clickable height.
